Yes. In this snapshot, `Path` exposes `copy`, and `preserve_metadata` defaults to `False`.

The `library/pathlib.rst` entry documents the signature as `Path.copy(target, *, follow_symlinks=True, preserve_metadata=False)`. It describes the method as copying a file or directory tree to the target and returning a new `Path` for it. The same file marks the method as new in 3.14 (`versionadded:: 3.14`). It also documents `Path.copy_into(target_dir, *, follow_symlinks=True, preserve_metadata=False)`, which handles its other arguments identically to `Path.copy`.

